{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the way at the inn.</b> Rashi explains: because he occupied himself with the lodging first. It implies from his commentary that he should have circumcised him before occupying himself with the lodging first. And the difficulty is that the next day he needed to depart and the child would be in danger. One may answer that that child was at the place of lodging after Aaron met him and said to him: 'over the earlier ones we grieve, and you come to add to them' — even though the tribe of Levi was not enslaved, nonetheless he would not want them to come to a place where Israel would see affliction. And Tziporah and her sons returned from there. If so, since it was in their mind to return, he could have circumcised him before occupying himself with the lodging, and Tziporah would wait there until the child recovered from his circumcision. Therefore he was punished."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:43.207973376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}